  notes    = "Offset of mce::MaterialPtr ItemInHandRenderer::mMatBlendBlock: 1D8h on 26.51 (header 472: ActorShaderManager 38h, two ItemStack, then the materials from 198h), the material that the ghost draws with. The ItemInHandRenderer constructor is the only function that loads the entity_alphablend_nocolor text; it builds each material from its name and stores it in member order: entity_alphablend (FNV hash B6D69B17EEBE1A1Eh) goes to this+1D8h and entity_alphablend_nocolor to +1E8h. For each material it moves the hash, calls the material lookup and stores the material pointer (`mov rdx,[rbp+..]; mov rcx,[rbp+..]; mov [rdx+1D8h],rcx`). The recipe finds the constructor by that text and reads the store displacement. The recipe starts at that store (`mov [rdx+disp],rcx`, offset 0) and runs forward over the two shared_ptr releases and the name string release to the setup of the next material, entity_alphablend_nocolor (`lea r9,[rip+..]; mov edx,19h`); the name length 19h is the one kept byte, and it picks the store before it. It is one pattern_any with one alternative per shape (the frame offsets of the 26.60 constructor take disp32 forms). Range window 1C8h..1E8h. Value 1D8h on 26.51, 1E0h on 26.60. What changed in 6ad79ee4-17d51891a1119914 (26.60): the member moved by 8h, the constructor adds a nop after each direct call, and its temporaries moved to frame offsets above 80h, so the 26.51 pattern (from the hash load over the lookup call to the store) did not match; no common alignment from the hash to the store exists on both builds, so the anchor moved to the bytes after the store. The value is read as an offset by the mod; no mirror. Would have survived with a better recipe."

